  "body": "See https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/2056#issuecomment-261513957\r\n\r\nThe current [Parsing XHTML documents](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/xhtml.html#parsing-xhtml-documents), [Serializing XHTML fragments](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/xhtml.html#serialising-xhtml-fragments), and [Parsing XHTML fragments](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/xhtml.html#parsing-xhtml-fragments) sections define requirements for _XML_ processing, not anything specific to “XHTML”.\r\n\r\nAnd in general continued use of the term “the XHTML syntax” buys us nothing at this point, so the change in this PR replaces all references to that with just “XML”.\r\n\r\nWhen most authors see the term “XHTML document” they think about XHTML1, not about anything we define in the current HTML spec. It’s ambiguous. So this change clears away that ambiguity.",
